@startuml
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBorderColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #ECF0F1
}

title Mass Edit Cycle (MassEditWizard): Differential Review and Atomic Persistence

actor "Administrator" as Admin
participant "MassEditWizard" as Wizard
participant "EditFormGenerator" as Form
participant "ReviewModal" as Review
participant "BaseRestController" as Controller
participant "BaseService" as Service
participant "BaseRepository" as Repo

== 1. Version History Initialization ==

Wizard -> Wizard: Initializes edit history (original, versions, activeVersion)
activate Wizard

== 2. Sequential Editing with Version History (Undo / Redo) ==

loop For each selected item (activeIndex = 0 .. N-1)
    Wizard -> Form: Render form with active entity
    Admin -> Form: Modifies fields and clicks "Update & Next"
    Form -> Wizard: applyUpdate(updatedEntity)

    Wizard -> Wizard: Records changes in history
    note right of Wizard
        Manages versions and the
        active version in memory.
        See activity diagram:
        "19_Flow_MassEditWizard_UndoRedo_History"
    end note
end

== 3. Differential Change Review (ReviewModal) ==

Admin -> Wizard: Clicks "Review" button
Wizard -> Review: Opens comparative modal passing originals[] and updated[]
activate Review

Review -> Admin: Displays field-by-field differential comparison
Admin -> Review: Reviews diffs and clicks "Confirm Changes"

Review -> Wizard: onConfirm()
deactivate Review

== 4. Batch Submission and Atomic Backend Persistence ==

Wizard -> Wizard: Retrieves confirmed edits (activeVersion >= 0)

Wizard -> Controller: PUT /api/v1/resource/some\n[Payload: UpdateSomeDTO { ids: [...], entities: [...] }]
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: updateSome(request.getIds(), request.getEntities())
activate Service

Service -> Service: Validates size parity: ids.size() == updatedEntities.size()
note right of Service
  Atomic transactional execution (@Transactional).
  Checks existence, invokes hook updateEntityFields
  and triggers rollback if any item fails.
  See activity diagram:
  "17_Flow_BaseService_updateSome_Transactional"
end note

loop For each id and entity in batch
    Service -> Repo: findById(id)
    Service -> Service: updateEntityFields(existing, updated)
    Service -> Service: toSave.add(existing)
end

Service -> Repo: saveAll(toSave)
activate Repo
Repo --> Service: savedEntities: List<T>
deactivate Repo

Service --> Controller: savedEntities
deactivate Service

Controller --> Wizard: 200 OK [JSON with persisted entities]
deactivate Controller

Wizard --> Admin: Closes modal and refreshes ListGenerator table with consolidated data
deactivate Wizard

@enduml
